    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on high-ceiling leadoff hitters facing exploitable arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) secures the top spot in our lineup, driven by a favorable park factor (+16%) and a significant boost from facing a slower pitcher, which aligns perfectly with our need to prioritize stolen bases. He is joined by **Trea Turner** (75.29) and **Christian Yelich** (72.22) as our primary drivers; **Christian Yelich** benefits from a massive +13% platoon edge and a slow opposing delivery that increases his SB potential against Andre Pallante. While **Kyle Schwarber** (71.49) rounds out our elite tier, he remains a high-variance play who relies heavily on his ability to leverage the +12% SP skill advantage against Brady Singer to produce power metrics despite being a right-on-right matchup.\n\nThe bench decision for today was particularly tight, with **Lars Nootbaar** (38.93) narrowly missing the cut. While **Lars Nootbaar** offers strong xwOBA potential, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to a poor matchup against Logan Henderson, whose sub-3.00 xERA creates a significant drag on his projection. We are proceeding cautiously with several spots as we await official word on **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Trea Turner**, **Luke Raley**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; because these players are currently listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" our projections assume specific spots that, if altered, could shift their efficiency scores by several points. \n\nWe are monitoring **Junior Caminero** (61.45) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) as steady mid-tier contributors. **Casey Schmitt** is particularly interesting today, as he receives a rare +11% dynamic platoon boost and a +5% wind-out advantage that elevates him into \"Strong\" start territory. Conversely, we are keeping **Carson Benge** (57.41) and **Gary Sanchez** (48.18) on short leashes; **Gary Sanchez** is currently our lowest-rated starter, and we remain ready to swap in high-upside bench options like **Nelson Velazquez** or **Dillon Dingler** should late-breaking lineup changes negatively impact our current roster configuration. The focus remains on maximizing volume and speed to compensate for the relative scarcity of stolen base opportunities across the rest of the league.",
